+## 4. Review001 remediation
+
+The single Owner-authorized remediation batch closes the review design gaps:
+
+- final runs bind HEAD plus a byte-exact binary patch, changed-path inventory,
+  and path/size/SHA-256 identity for every untracked source file;
+- the Python 3.12 bootstrap and CI quality job explicitly synchronize the
+  dedicated retrieval group while the production default remains unchanged;
+- only `evaluation/results/nfcorpus-real-final/` is trackable; dataset bytes and
+  historical `nfcorpus-real-run-001` remain ignored;
+- missing/empty/non-evaluable qrels and incomplete or non-recomputable results
+  fail closed before artifacts are written;
+- dependency tests and dependency-audit evidence bind exact retrieval pins;
+- serial query execution, one requested BLAS thread, runtime thread metadata,
+  and latency limitations are recorded; hybrid build timing is derived and
+  labelled separately from measured sparse/dense timing;
+- each record saves its full candidate pool and complete component ranks/scores;
+  contract tests reconstruct RRF top ten from those artifacts.
+
+Final real metrics and artifact hashes are intentionally not copied from the
+immutable historical run. The parent lifecycle must run the final command with
+`--run-id nfcorpus-real-final`, then update this record from those exact bytes.
